# stow-ignores/omarchy — baseline patterns plus everything Omarchy 4 already
# manages itself. Stowing our own copies over these either hijacks Omarchy's
# live config/theme engine or gets silently overwritten by it later. Verified
# by hand against a fresh Omarchy 4.0.0 install (Hyprland 0.56.2) — see the
# comment on each entry for the exact mechanism.
#
# Selected interactively by do-stow.sh / do-unstow.sh (fzf profile picker).

.ssh/

# Hyprland: Omarchy 4's real config entrypoint is
# ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua, which require()s monitors/input/bindings/
# looknfeel/autostart.lua siblings in the same directory. Hyprland 0.56.2
# still honors a legacy hyprland.conf if one is present (deprecated, removed
# in 0.57) — no filename collides, so stow would merge our old .conf-based
# package in silently, and Hyprland may pick it up over the .lua config,
# replacing Omarchy's entire session setup. Ignore the whole package.
.config/hypr/

# Neovim: Omarchy ships its own LazyVim distro with a dynamically
# hot-reloaded colorscheme (lua/plugins/theme.lua, regenerated per Omarchy
# theme switch, + a theme-hotreload watcher plugin). Our
# nvim/lua/plugins/catppuccin.lua is a second lazy.nvim spec at the same
# priority=1000 that hardcodes `colorscheme "catppuccin"` — no filename
# collides in lua/plugins/, so it would load alongside Omarchy's and fight
# it for the active colorscheme on every startup/reload. init.lua and
# lazy-lock.json also collide directly (real files, blocks stow outright).
.config/nvim/

# Terminal emulators: Omarchy wires these into its live theme system via an
# include/import that points at ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme/*.
# Stowing our own file replaces that hook, so theme switching silently stops
# updating the terminal's colors.
.config/alacritty/alacritty.toml
.config/ghostty/
.config/kitty/

# Fontconfig: `omarchy-font-set` writes directly to
# ~/.config/fontconfig/fonts.conf on every font change (`cat > "$file"`,
# not a symlink swap). If that path is a symlink into this repo, Omarchy
# silently overwrites our tracked file the next time the font changes.
.config/fontconfig/

.config/rofi
.config/waybar
.config/matugen
.config/swaync
